## Test Smell Audit — Academic Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10)  
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class is marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Total    | 4           | 4              |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)  
**Rationale:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` introduces 3 seconds of non-deterministic wait. Even in integration tests, this remains a smell — it makes the suite slow and the pass/fail threshold arbitrary.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));

// ✅ Fix — poll with timeout
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(50, cts.Token);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures on slow CI; wastes 3 s per run even when the event fires in 10 ms.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)  
**Rationale:** `if/else` means one assertion branch never executes — you have no idea which path ran in a green build.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
else
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);

// ✅ Fix — split into explicit tests or assert deterministically
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
// If PremiumUser path matters, write a second test that arranges a PremiumUser.
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden testing gap — if the type hierarchy changes, one branch silently stops executing.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)  
**Rationale:** Inserts 100 rows but never verifies any outcome. MSTest reports PASS simply because no exception is thrown.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

// ✅ Fix — verify the side effect
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

Assert.AreEqual(100, _repository.ListAll().Count);
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — if `Insert` silently drops rows, this test still passes.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)  
**Rationale:** 4 assertions with no message parameters. When one fails, the MSTest runner reports only the assertion type and expected/actual — you must read the code to determine *which* property was wrong.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);

// ✅ Fix — add discriminating messages
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slow diagnosis during CI failures — especially in parallel test runs with terse output.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

| Test | Notes |
|------|-------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior, clean null-check assertion |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count is self-documenting (3 inserts → 3 expected) |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good concurrency smoke test with assertion |

The **General Fixture** smell does *not* apply — both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test method.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Why First |
|----------|-------|-----------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~1 min | Prevents false-pass today |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Eliminates hidden gap |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~10 min | Removes flakiness + speeds CI by 3 s |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | ~2 min | Improves diagnostics |

**Overall verdict:** 5 of 7 tests (71%) are well-structured. The three high-severity smells are localized and straightforward to fix — a short refactoring session would bring this suite to a clean bill of health.
